WEBVTT

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.180
Can't sleep?

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.000
Hey, um...

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.860
You aren't suspicious?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.190
That I might have lured
 you to the Arbiter?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.780
I mean, you didn't, did you?

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.760
N-No, but...

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.260
Jeez,

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.130
Kudo and Professor Los don't 
seem to doubt me, either.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.040
You're all too nice!

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.020
It makes me worried about 
the future of mages!

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.760
I feel like "unconcerned" is
 more accurate than "nice."

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.020
Be more concerned with other people!

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.530
So you want to be blamed?

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.060
No, I just...

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.660
Feel right here.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.680
Is this an antler?

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.280
Because of my antlers,
 I was called the child of a demon.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.740
I grew up being told to serve the 
Church to cleanse my tainted soul.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.710
That's awful.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:24.300
But when I studied beastfallen 
at the Academy,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.390
I realized I might be one.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.920
A beastfallen is...

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:35.030
..."what results when a witch bestows the soul 
of a beast upon a warrior who seeks strength."

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:37.780
Yup! That's it!

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.600
If the beast warrior and the witch die,
 the beast soul has nowhere to go

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.120
and enters the witch's bloodline.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.960
Then part-beast, part-human babies 
appear among the witch's descendants.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.400
Over time, as the witch blood dilutes,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.200
the beast soul's influence gradually weakens,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.640
resulting in an increasingly 
human appearance.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.890
Professor Los just told 
me that I'm a beastfallen.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.640
I felt so relieved when I heard that.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.520
I was able to feel relieved,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.150
thanks to you.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.260
Me?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:19.610
You wouldn't speak ill of Kudo 
because he's a beastfallen.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.160
That made me happy.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.160
I only...

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.830
said how I felt...

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.840
I'm going to bed now!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:41.660
Okay.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.050
You should go to bed soon, too, Sayb!

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.580
She would have let you put 
the moves on her just now.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:52.930
Professor Los?

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.710
What hast thou so timid?

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.990
I don't really get it.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.740
Get what?

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.860
Love and stuff.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.620
How quaint!

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.420
Well, lad, worry, suffer, 
and flail thy way forward!

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.760
The more you three struggle,

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.500
the more entertaining things are for me!

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.010
<i>That's really warped.</i>

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.680
Episode 3
Beyond the Steam

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:57.230
I told you it was risky to 
get in bed with the Church!

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.400
Please don't expel me... 
Please don't expel me...

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.060
Damn it! All for some chump change!

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.170
So those two were leaking info?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.320
Those jerks.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.780
Well, that is that.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.290
As for what is next,

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.030
we shall continue the journey
 with just the four of us.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.290
But first... Kudo.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:21.050
I expect daily life will be a 
struggle with thy hands like that.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.300
Let us grow some!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.110
Don't say that so lightly!

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.150
I ain't some bean sprout in the shade!

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.300
Thou hast healing magic, 
dost thou not?

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:34.310
To my knowledge, magic ought to 
be organized into four chapters.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.110
The Chapter of Hunting, 
conceived for hunting;

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.980
the Chapter of Harvest, for agriculture;

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.840
the Chapter of Capture, for public order;

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.820
and the Chapter of Protection, for healing.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.970
Impressive! You know so much!

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:53.080
I have been passionate about
 <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i> for many years.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:59.080
The textbook you three use is a version of 
the <i>Grimoire</i> edited to be safer, is it not?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.710
I can't do it!

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:04.760
Spells from the Chapter of 
Protection use the most magic!

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.680
I'll run out of magic and collapse 
before the fingers form.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.680
But thou hast Sayb.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:13.790
Of course!

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.430
With Sayb here, we can use 
all the magic we want! Wow!

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:19.360
I see.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.360
So? Which of you is best at 
the Chapter of Protection?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.350
Kudo is.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:25.820
What?!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.820
M-My specialties are Hunting and Capture!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:33.170
I heard people make fun of 
you for being bad at Hunting.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.630
Don't remember such stupid stuf—

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.080
Damn it! What do I need to do?

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:44.560
The most efficient way is to touch a mucous 
membrane where blood vessels can be felt.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:46.550
To kiss, for example.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:47.550
K—

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.550
Kiss?

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.150
No, no, no!

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.300
Absolutely not!

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.920
Through the hands, then.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.310
I shall regulate the flow.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.720
'Twould not be pretty if this went afoul.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:04.380
Huh?

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:11.320
Excessive magic would cause blood to spray 
from every opening in the body, then death.

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.000
Let us begin.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:25.750
Hey, wai—

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:27.210
<i>Here?</i>

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.640
Concentrate.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.440
Well? Dost thou feel the flow?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.060
Kudo, the incantation.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.000
Kudo?

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.460
Hey, it's not just me, right?

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:55.390
Who's... e-e-embarrassed to chant 
incantations in front of people?

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.520
I understand. It <i>is</i> embarrassing.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.790
Don't say that! I'm trying 
not to think about it!

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.530
Ridiculous! Incantations are cool!

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.790
Now, gird thyself!

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.210
Iea Do Kouha!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.550
Blood, race forth!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.270
Become flesh and return!

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.600
Chapter of Protection,

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.180
verse one!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:18.350
Chordia!

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:27.190
Amazing! His hand is regenerating!

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:30.650
Pipe down! I'm concentrating here!

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.080
Grant me power!

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.940
My name is Kudo!

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.890
Whoa! They've regenerated!

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.210
Wow! He just grew new hands!

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:02.350
They built an academy for magic, right?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.850
I'd love to go there.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:06.670
Now, bard, sing!

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.870
A song in praise of mages!

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:20.580
Half the people hate mages. Half love them.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.500
Acclaim on par with the threat 
against your lives awaits you three.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:30.000
You have already experienced 
the greatest persecution.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.590
'Tis fine to seek abundant praise!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.510
Now, we must be off, my ducklings!

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.030
Stand tall! Hold your heads high!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:45.370
The Kingdom of Wenias's prized 
mages are coming through!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.380
I see.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.660
A city!

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:04.500
This is a large city.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.410
It's much smaller than Plasta.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.890
Move it! Move it!

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:11.770
You're in the way!

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.220
S-Sayb!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.130
Huh?

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:22.880
Yikes.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.120
Are you okay?

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.770
First up is a bath.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:31.060
My usual inn boasts 
large bathing facilities.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.280
B-Bathing facilities?

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:36.680
Would I be able to use them?

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:37.820
What do you mean?

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:40.820
Duh. She doesn't want her antlers seen.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.070
'Tis fine. I shall make a reservation.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.580
Thou canst let thy hair down without worry.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.500
This is incredible!

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.260
Hey, um, before you were with us,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.930
we discussed our reasons 
for becoming mages...

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.060
To join the Church & Mage Army.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:11.420
Do you have to be a mage to join?

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:15.070
You really don't know anything, do you?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:19.820
The Church & Mage Army was originally 
called the Church Knights.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.570
It was a collection of knights who 
forsook all their worldly possessions

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:26.100
just to protect the Church and the people.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.210
And the Church disliked beastfallen.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.910
After peace was made with 
witches, it was renamed,

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:36.160
and a beastfallen unit was formed.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:38.090
The elite of the elite.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.090
But, you see, I'm not strong.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:44.040
If I want to join the
 Church & Mage Army,

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.590
becoming a mage is my only shot.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.850
Why do you want to join them?

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:54.490
Have you heard of the
 Dragon Conqueror King?

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.360
Yeah.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:58.890
I used to be in a freak show.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:02.360
While I was there, we were hit 
by the Disasters of the North.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:05.540
That stuff that happened six years ago?

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:10.410
Some crazy witch suddenly
 declared she'd destroy the world,

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.620
and the north was brought to ruin in a night.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:18.250
Even now the north is crawling with monsters, 
and the Church & Mage Army fights them.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:21.940
At the time, the Church & Mage Army
 was still the Church Knights.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:28.030
To the world, I was an embodiment of 
corruption. A worthless beastfallen.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:32.650
And so, the fact is, 
he didn't have to save me.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:37.320
Yet he found me and smiled.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.700
Good. You're alive.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.110
I wanted to be like him.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:48.440
Peace was made with witches and the name
 was changed to the Church & Mage Army.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:51.500
The Dragon Conqueror King 
became their symbol,

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.510
so I made the Army my goal.

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:58.780
I see. That's kind of amazing.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.160
What about you?

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.510
Huh?

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.600
Why do you wanna be a mage?

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.270
You're just gonna leave me hanging?

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:07.010
Oh...

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:08.530
I—

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:12.050
What do you think of these baths?

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.750
Spacious, yes? Lavish, yes? 
Incredible, are they not?

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:19.430
P-P-Professor Los?!

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.440
What's going on in your skull?!

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.550
I am here to bathe.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:23.840
Go to the women's bath!

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.900
Scram, you pervert!

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:27.320
Pervert?!

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:31.700
Why must I be treated as a pervert 
for removing my clothes at the baths?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:35.290
Just 100 years ago, 'twas perfectly 
normal to bathe in mixed company!

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:39.370
I swear, adolescents are so overly sensitive.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:44.550
Does seeing my beautiful 
flesh roil your lower halves?

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:48.070
Very well! Roil away!

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:51.350
Who would be roiled by you, moron?!

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:53.840
H-Hey, wait.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.050
So sorry! T-Take this!

00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:14.540
Huh?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.050
Ah! A monster!

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:29.530
Yeah, to be honest,
 I think it's a monster, too.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:34.850
You know, I think an apology takes 
priority over saying stupid stuff.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.520
<i>The journey from that point on</i>

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:43.020
<i>went so smoothly that the disastrous 
beginning hardly seemed real.</i>

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:47.250
<i>The inn owners along the road 
all knew Professor Los,</i>

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.530
<i>and they welcomed </i>us<i> as well.</i>

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:53.160
<i>Professor Los knew where 
to find the clearest lakes,</i>

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.740
<i>the best camping spots,
 and the shadiest trees.</i>

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.210
<i>She even taught us hunting methods for fun.</i>

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.210
<i>And when we encountered 
people who needed help,</i>

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.770
<i>she actively encouraged us to use magic.</i>

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.670
<i>In my three years at the Academy,</i>

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:16.470
<i>never had I felt so strongly safeguarded.</i>

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:20.670
Professor Los, it's kinda 
like you're our mom.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.640
Your mom?!

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.230
What art thou? A needy child?

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.940
But if we seek attention, 
you'll let us have it.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.200
Hey, now.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:34.650
Hey, Professor, what are you gonna 
do when this escort job is over?

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.990
I shall go see the Mud-Black Witch.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:39.960
The Mud-Black... You mean...?

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:46.210
Precisely. The inventor of magic and 
the author of <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i>.

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:47.930
But...

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:48.960
...yes.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:52.970
I could let you meet the 
author of the grimoire.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.110
Then what?

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:56.440
We shall talk!

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.970
I don't see the point.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.850
Why, it will stave off boredom.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.790
I get so bored I cannot stand it.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:07.980
After living for 300 years, 
I have grown tired even of breathing.

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:13.360
But as long as my dear Ludens exists, 
my life shall know no end.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:20.170
Listen, Kudo. A witch who sustains herself 
on magic loses even the need for food.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.000
Dost thou grasp what that means?

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.000
It's super convenient?

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.390
Thou art not wrong.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:31.380
Living things spend most of their 
time eating and sleeping.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.600
However, I shan't die if I do not eat.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.140
Therefore, meals are meaningless. As is sleep.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.520
Nor do I need to produce offspring.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.960
So love and romance too are meaningless.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:47.020
Answer me this. What is it that I have left?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.180
Huh? Um...

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.780
Is it... play?

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:54.210
Yes! Precisely!

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:55.780
I'm right?! Woo-hoo!

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:58.170
Fun!

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:00.910
<i>That</i> is everything to me.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.290
New experiences, grave dangers!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:08.570
To me, even the collapse of the north 
that plunged the world into fear

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:11.190
was entertainment that
 made my heart dance.

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:14.920
Seeing the pack of demons 
trampling humanity,

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.700
this thought leapt to mind:

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:20.560
"Ah, I'm glad I lived to see this!"

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.430
You've got a screw loose.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.740
"Normal" changes with the times.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:31.640
Witches who have lived through hundreds
 of years and many kinds of "normal"

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:34.190
lose their sense of "normal", as well.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:36.490
Still,

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:39.860
I think you're a good person, 
Professor Los.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:44.160
A-Art thou trying to make me blush?

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.160
Anyway,

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.880
I recently realized something.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.040
'Tis fun to spend time with people.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.430
No two people are alike.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:58.180
This journey with you 
is especially enjoyable,

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.880
but the journey shall end soon.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.060
'Tis not far to our destination.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.740
What're you people doing?

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.940
You can't be there!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.820
Who art thou?

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.230
Hide!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.650
Hurry up and run!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:18.280
If he finds you, you'll be killed!

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.660
Hurry! Hurry!

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.410
Come. In here.

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:27.100
Go inside! Hurry!

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.160
Centipede,

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.180
thunder,

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.380
eye of bird...

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.130
Gate, seal!

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:47.110
Didst thou just use sorcery?

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:50.670
Shh! The barrier doesn't block sound.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:58.400
This barrier is constructed so as to 
use particular words to activate.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.910
What precision.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.910
Tell us. Did a witch of the 
village set up this barrier?

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.380
Hey!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.970
Where are you hiding?

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:18.050
If you come out now, you won't be punished.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:25.650
If you don't, I'll break the other 
kids' legs. Is that what you want?

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.060
Stay put.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:35.860
That's strange. I hear heartbeats...

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.360
right around here.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:47.290
Don't!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.260
Ah. There you are.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.680
What do we do? He jumped out!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.040
With magic, we can take him!

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:08.680
Hort, get him! You have Saybil with you.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:13.100
I see. You're part of the field program.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.960
H-How do you know that?

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.190
Who knows?

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:19.260
You should know that you won't 
finish an incantation in time.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.190
You're too close to me.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:25.360
One of you should've hidden and cast fro—

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:41.760
Run!

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.680
Wilt thou not chase?

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:52.100
Don't be ridiculous.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:57.190
The moment I turn my back to you, 
my ass can kiss my tail goodbye.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:01.320
Oh, thou wilt retreat?

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:06.660
I'm a mercenary. I don't 
fight battles I can't win.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:11.080
Even so, there is no reason 
for <i>me</i> to let <i>you</i> go.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:15.780
I see.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:21.420
If I kill you, someone 
else will act. Is that it?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.840
You saved me the trouble of explaining.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:27.430
I just needed the kid to 
return to the village.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:31.930
But what about you? They went 
running toward the village.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.630
Your field program students.

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:40.900
The Staff of Ludens, eh? A fine staff.

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:43.260
How much dost thou know?

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.710
Go after your precious students.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.910
We'll meet again.

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:05.380
Father, I'm back!

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:07.100
Laios.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:12.000
I was worried. You just disappeared.

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:16.270
Those people saved me.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:18.110
They said they're mages!

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:24.060
You three are mages?

00:23:55.010 --> 00:24:09.990
<b>Next Episode       "I'm not Afraid to Die"</b>

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:59.140
So fluffy! I want him, too!

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:01.830
No. He is <i>my </i>mercenary.

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:04.130
Huh? And who art <i>thou</i>?

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:07.300
Next Episode: "I'm Not Afraid to Die."

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.610
Tell me who!
